# Mainnet ceremony environment: the PAXG-first launch (docs/ORACLE_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md).
# Copy to .env.mainnet (gitignored), fill in every placeholder in angle brackets, have a second
# person read every line back, then load it in the shell:
#   set -a; source .env.mainnet; set +a
# The ceremony is one step: the preflight, then the deploy.
#   npx hardhat run scripts/preflight-mainnet.ts --network mainnet
#   npx hardhat run scripts/deploy.ts --network mainnet
# The oracle prices on Chainlink PAXG/USD and XAU/USD alone. There is no pool source and no market
# feed step: PAXG_CONFIRM_FEED, XAUT_CONFIRM_FEED, PAXG_AGREEMENT_BAND_PPM and MARKET_FEEDS are
# retired, and the preflight and deploy.ts refuse an environment that still sets any of them.
# The preflight parses every value below with the same code deploy.ts uses, bounds each
# parameter by the contracts' own limits, checks the addresses against the live chain, prints
# the effective set and writes deployments/mainnet.preflight.json; deploy.ts refuses to run
# unless that record exists and matches what it parsed itself. The record is good for 60 minutes
# of chain time, and deploy.ts reads the three Safes again and refuses if a threshold or an owner
# differs from the record: run the preflight, then the deploy, in one sitting.
#
# No mainnet deployment until every launch blocker in the plan's section 6 is closed. The numbers
# below are the economic model's (docs/ORACLE_MANIPULATION_MODEL.md section 14.1 item 6).

# --- Only you can supply these six, the token address pair below them, and the operations Safe further down ---
RPC_URL="<mainnet RPC URL, your own Alchemy or Infura endpoint>"
PRIVATE_KEY="<deployer key: fresh, single-use, hardware-wallet derived, funded with ETH>"
TIMELOCK_PROPOSER="<proposer Safe, 2-of-3>"
TIMELOCK_EXECUTOR="<executor Safe, 2-of-3: executes matured proposals>"
TIMELOCK_GUARDIAN="<guardian Safe, 2-of-3: pause, per-token freeze and unfreeze only>"
ETHERSCAN_API_KEY="<Etherscan API key, for scripts/verify-etherscan.ts>"
# The address GSUSD is created at, and the CREATE2 salt that gives it. Both are required on
# mainnet. The address follows from the deployer's address and nonce, the salt and the token's
# creation code; the preflight (gsusd:address) and deploy.ts refuse a pair that does not agree.
# scripts/lib/stablecoinAddress.ts says how a salt is found. A new deployer key means a new salt.
GSUSD_SALT="<32 byte salt found for this deployer>"
GSUSD_ADDRESS="<the address that salt gives>"
# The deployer must not be an owner of any of these Safes: the key is retired after the ceremony,
# and the preflight fails (safe:deployer-not-owner) if it finds it among a Safe's owners.
# The executor is a Safe. The zero address instead would let anyone execute every matured
# proposal, at a moment of their choosing within the timelock's 7 day grace period, so an approval
# made for one incident could land in the next. The preflight and deploy.ts refuse it on mainnet
# unless the line below is uncommented as well; accept it only with a written reason, and then the
# proposer Safe must cancel every operation that is superseded, reverted or no longer wanted
# (docs/LAUNCH.md, executor policy).
# ALLOW_OPEN_EXECUTOR=1

# --- The operations Safe: receives surplus withdrawals, holds no role in any contract ---
# Not wired into the deployment and not part of the parameters hash. When set, the preflight
# checks that it has code, answers as a Safe and differs from the three Safes above and from the
# deployer; left unset on mainnet, the preflight warns. scripts/withdraw-surplus.ts refuses to
# pay a governance Safe or the deployer.
OPERATIONS_SAFE="<operations Safe: a fourth Safe, distinct from the three above>"

# --- Published inventory (docs/ORACLES.md section 1). Do not edit; the preflight refuses a change. ---
PAXG_TOKEN=0x45804880De22913dAFE09f4980848ECE6EcbAf78
XAUT_TOKEN=0x68749665FF8D2d112Fa859AA293F07A622782F38
# G: Chainlink XAU/USD, the gold reference. Mandatory, and never a token's market price.
XAU_USD_ANCHOR_FEED=0x214eD9Da11D2fbe465a6fc601a91E62EbEc1a0D6
# C: Chainlink PAXG/USD, PAXG's timely market price (8 decimals, 24 h heartbeat).
PAXG_FEED=0x9944D86CEB9160aF5C5feB251FD671923323f8C3

# --- PAXG's gold band and liquidation cap (plan section 3) ---
# The gold band g: borrowing and reserve swaps need C within this of G, measured against G (plan:
# 2%; measured maximum 0.84%). GoldOracle bounds it to 5000..100000 ppm.
# The liquidation cap m: the liquidation price is min(max(C, G), G x (1 + m)), so a push of C down
# values PAXG at gold at worst and a push up gains at most m (plan: 2%). GoldOracle bounds it to
# 5000..50000 ppm, and the preflight also requires it below the headroom PAXG_LIQ_RATIO leaves above
# par (10% at 110%). Both change later only through a timelocked governance proposal.
PAXG_GOLD_BAND_PPM=20000
PAXG_LIQUIDATION_CLAMP_PPM=20000

# --- XAUT: registered, inactive ---
# The oracle constructor registers XAUT (its address is an immutable), so XAUT needs a feed. Leave
# XAUT_FEED unset: deploy.ts creates an InactiveFeed (8 decimals, description "Inactive", an
# all-zero round) and registers XAUT on it, so XAUT prices nothing ("No reliable price"). The
# XAU/USD address cannot serve: GoldOracle.setAnchorFeed refuses an anchor a token uses as its
# feed. Nothing else about XAUT is configured: no collateral type, stability fee, reserve asset or
# stability pool token. Under LAUNCH_CAPS=open (and backstop) the preflight and deploy.ts refuse
# XAUT_DEBT_CEILING, XAUT_MIN_RATIO, XAUT_LIQ_RATIO, XAUT_LIQ_PENALTY, XAUT_STABILITY_FEE_BPS and
# RESERVE_MIN_RESERVE_XAUT. Activation is a later governance batch (docs/LAUNCH.md, XAUT activation).

# --- Launch policy (docs/LAUNCH.md step 3.2). The preflight and deploy.ts both enforce these. ---
# LAUNCH_CAPS=open is the mainnet launch profile (the project decision of 29 October 2026): no
# debt ceiling and no per-block mint cap, PAXG the only active collateral and XAUT dormant.
# Leave PAXG_DEBT_CEILING unset (or "unlimited") and PER_BLOCK_MINT_CAP unset (or 0); any other
# value is refused.
LAUNCH_CAPS=open
# LAUNCH_CAPS=backstop is refused on mainnet by the preflight, deploy.ts and verify-deployment.ts;
# it exists for forks and local rehearsals only. It is the same PAXG-first shape with PAXG under
# one debt ceiling (above zero, at most PAXG_BACKSTOP_MAX in scripts/lib/launchEnv.ts, 5,000,000
# GSUSD) and the per-block cap armed. That maximum was derived under the retired pool design
# (section 14.1 item 6) and has not been re-derived for the two source rules. Never put
# LAUNCH_CAPS=backstop, PAXG_DEBT_CEILING or PAXG_BACKSTOP_REHEARSAL_MAX (the rehearsal stand-in
# for the maximum) in .env.mainnet.
# The guarded profile (both tokens active, the default when LAUNCH_CAPS is unset) is for
# testnets and the end-to-end harness only; the preflight and a mainnet deploy refuse it.
# 25 hours: the feeds' 24 h heartbeat plus grace; the oracle caps the value here
STALENESS_THRESHOLD=90000
# Stays 0. The 2% reserve floor is automatic: SurplusBuffer keeps 2% of max(live supply, one day
# smoothed supply) by itself, so no governance step raises it. This is only an optional higher
# governed minimum, set later through the timelock with scripts/set-min-reserve.ts if ever wanted;
# the preflight refuses any other value at deploy.
MIN_GSUSD_RESERVE=0
# Smallest vault debt, 1,000 GSUSD; the preflight refuses any other value on mainnet. The
# liquidator keeps 60% of the 5% penalty, 3% of the debt repaid, and at mainnet gas that share
# on a 1,000 GSUSD vault is what makes the smallest liquidation worth sending. The testnet
# harness uses 100.
MIN_DEBT_GSUSD=1000

# --- Defaults deploy.ts applies when unset, listed so the ceremony record is complete ---
# Leave a line commented out to take the default; an empty value (KEY=) is refused, never
# read as zero. Every value is bounded by the contract that receives it, and the preflight
# prints the whole effective set. XAUT has no lines here: it is dormant.
# SILO_CAP=100000000000000000000
# PAXG_MIN_RATIO=1300000
# PAXG_LIQ_RATIO=1100000
# PAXG_LIQ_PENALTY=50000
# PAXG_STABILITY_FEE_BPS=200
# BAD_DEBT_PAUSE_THRESHOLD=25000000000000000000000
# PER_BLOCK_MINT_CAP: 0 under open (the default there; any other value is refused).
# RESERVE_PENALTY_SHARE_BPS=4000
# ORIGINATION_FEE_BPS=5 (taken from what each mint delivers; 0 to 100, launch policy 5)
# UNDERWATER_DISCOUNT_PPM=20000
# RESERVE_DAILY_CAP_PPM=200000
# RESERVE_MIN_RESERVE_PAXG=0
# RESERVE_AGGREGATE_DAILY_CAP_USD=0
# MIN_COLLATERAL_RESERVE=0 (the buffer's gold minimum for PAXG, in the token's smallest unit)
# SILO_LOCK_VAULT_ROLE=true (the silo factory's vault role is locked at deploy; leave it)
